course: dictionary
lesson: 15930
title: Unrealistic: not likely, not true to life
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unrealistic means not sensible or likely to happen, especially about plans or hopes. It can also mean not looking or seeming real or true to life. Break it into parts: un- means not, and realistic means sensible and possible.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «Tom's plan to build a whole house in one afternoon was unrealistic.» Building a house takes many weeks, so one afternoon is not likely. Ask yourself: could this really happen? If not, unrealistic is a good word to use.
explain: Unrealistic can describe a picture or a film too. «The film showed a cat driving a car and talking to the driver.» That is not true to life, so the scene is unrealistic. In maths, an answer can be unrealistic as well: a child who is 15 metres tall means the working needs checking.
fact: Unrealistic is an adjective: unrealistic, more unrealistic, most unrealistic.
fact: «Unrealistic» means not sensible or likely to happen, especially about plans or hopes.
fact: «Unrealistic» can also mean not looking or seeming real or true to life, as in an unrealistic film scene.
fact: Phrases you may meet: «unrealistic expectations», «an unrealistic goal», «totally unrealistic».
fact: The opposite of unrealistic is realistic, which means sensible and possible.
exercise: «Our goal of reading a whole library in one week is unrealistic.» What does unrealistic mean here? | Made of real stone | Very easy and quick | *Not likely to happen | Very happy about it
exercise: A film shows a dog flying over a city. Which word best describes this scene? | Glum | *Unrealistic | Barely | Famished
exercise: Which of these is an unrealistic goal? | Reading one book this week | Saving a little money each month | Learning to swim with practice | *Becoming a giant overnight
test: Which word is the opposite of unrealistic? | *Realistic | Silly | Glum | Ancient
test: In a fantasy film, a fish rides a bicycle through a shopping centre. Which word describes the scene best? | Curt | Luminous | *Unrealistic | Drooped
exam: Which sentence shows an unrealistic expectation? | Ben will practise the piano for ten minutes each day | Sam plans to read a chapter before bed | Priya will tidy her room on Saturday | *Ava expects to become a champion swimmer after one lesson
